hat's a big  problem the other problem that happens  is  tone tone is a really hard thing and i  don't think they talk about it enough  when they talk about writing creating a  consistent tone  is very difficult to do sometimes the  problem with the movie is that the tone  is all over the place one minute it's  funny and then  and it's trying to be scary and or or  it's not dramatic enough or so you don't  believe it because and if tone is  inconsistent you don't believe the thing  you're watching it does it starts to  become not real  and so that's that's another another  problem and then the other stuff falls  in under the heading of  of third act problems you know they  don't know how to end it or the third  act doesn't work and it's  more often than not because the first  act doesn't work because they haven't  established  good characters whenever i'm stuck  99 of the time it's because the people  aren't good enough  it's not because i can't make up where  to go i can't make up where to go  because the characters i've written  don't have enough to tell me  i don't know enough about them and i  always go back and i start thinking  about the people i'm writing about and  suddenly  20 ideas for scenes present themselves  you
 

